text:paper:1516831 {"content":"More on Systematic Error in a Boyle's Law Experiment\n\nA recent article1 in The Physics Teacher describes a method for analyzing a systematic error in a Boyle's law laboratory activity. Systematic errors are important to consider in physics labs because they tend to bias the results of measurements. There are numerous laboratory examples and resources that discuss this common source of error.2–7","paper_id":1516831}
